      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَتَّهُ</span></b> , [aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَتُ3َ</span></b> , accord to rule, and inf. n. app.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَتٌّ</span>, q. v.,] <i>He attributed</i> or <i>imputed to him,</i> or
<i>charged him with,</i> or <i>accused him of, a fault,</i> or
<i>defect,</i> or <i>the like;</i> as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَدَّهُ</span>; syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَابَهُ</span>. (TA.
[The sense in which <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عابه</span> is there used is indicated
by the context.])

